In <1993Mar3.160018.22349@porthos.cc.bellcore.com> dgob@blitzen.cc.bellcore.com (nortz,douglas m) writes:

>Hi. I just got NH3.1 from an ftp site. How do I set it up and how do I 
>transfer the files from my unix acct to my mac?

If you got the source, you can use tar and compress
to bundle all files and directories up properly, and
then transfer that file (in binary mode) to your Mac.

Use MacCompress to uncompress the file (DO NOT convert
newlines here)

Use MacTar to un-tar the file into all the folders and
files. CONVERT newlines at this stage.

Follow the instructions in :nh31:sys:mac:Install.mpw
(You need MPW C to compile it)

If you got the executable (.hqx file) you should just
send it using a network, tar floppy (readable by MacTar
and writable on most Sun workstations) or simple modem
transfer. Use StuffIt or Compact Pro or maybe BinHex4.0
to extract the archive from the hqx file, and you will
probably get a self-extracting archive that you just
double-click to install. You can then remove the .hqx
files and the self-extracting archive (keep a copy on
floppy!)

